# The model checkpoints. Several gigabytes each, they are not ours, and
# `python download_model.py` fetches whichever one this machine needs. See
# MODELS.md.
chkpt-mlx-int8/
chkpt-breeze-tts-2/
chkpt-full/
chkpt-mlx-int4/

# Local configuration: the language-model provider, API keys, the checkpoint
# path. Per-machine by definition, and .env.example is what belongs in the repo.
.env

# System-speech settings and the utterance archive: machine-local state.
state/

# Generated audio, and the log the server rewrites on every run. The blanket
# *.wav is a trap worth knowing about: it will silently swallow any audio
# fixture added to the repository later, so a test that needs one should write
# it at run time rather than ship it -- which is what test_voice_lock.py does.
outputs/
server.log
*.wav

# Virtual environments.
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Working notes and the reference documents this was built from. The README and
# MODELS.md are the documentation; these are drafts and scratch, and they are
# kept locally rather than published.
API.md
AUDIO_PLAYBACK.md
breezeTTS2 docs.md
GCLOUD_VERTEX_LLM_USAGE_GUIDE copy.md

# Build artefacts and Finder droppings: derived, and they churn on every run.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The voice library
#
# Recordings of real people and the profiles built from them: personal data,
# none of it reconstructable from source, so it stays on the machine that made
# it and is backed up separately. One voice is the exception -- it ships, so
# that a fresh clone has something to speak with before the user has recorded
# anything.
#
# These rules are last on purpose. Git applies the *last* matching pattern, so
# a negation placed above `*.wav` would be overruled by it, and the reference
# audio would silently not be committed while the profile beside it was. And
# the directory is excluded as `voices/*` rather than `voices/`, because git
# does not look inside an excluded directory at all -- a negation under one
# never matches.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
voices/*
!voices/voice_132150d40e9e455b97362ad6/
!voices/voice_132150d40e9e455b97362ad6/**
